Reject truncated bzip2 ZIP entries after compressed input is exhausted.

The private selector investigation found that UnZip's final output loop
repeatedly calls BZ2_bzDecompress with no input on a truncated selector
table.  The library correctly returns BZ_OK to request more input, but the
UnZip loop never terminates.  This loop predates the selector-count fix.

Adapt the EOF condition already used by upstream BZ2_bzRead in bzlib.c:
BZ_OK, no remaining input and spare output space mean unexpected EOF.
UnZip uses BZ_NO_STDIO, so its ZIP-entry reader must check this itself.
Keep draining full output buffers, and use the existing PK_ERR cleanup
path for incomplete streams.  This is a local UnZip integration change;
the bundled selector fix remains the upstream bzip2 1.0.8 implementation.

Review provenance: this is not a copied upstream UnZip commit or a Debian
UnZip patch.  It adapts the upstream bzip2 stdio reader's EOF rule to UnZip's
BZ_NO_STDIO ZIP-entry reader; the added extract.c hunk is local integration.

Download the authoritative bzip2 1.0.8 source release:
  https://sourceware.org/pub/bzip2/bzip2-1.0.8.tar.gz
Exact member: bzip2-1.0.8/bzlib.c
Function: BZ2_bzRead(), lines 1204-1206 in that release.
  gtar -xOf bzip2-1.0.8.tar.gz bzip2-1.0.8/bzlib.c | gsed -n '1199,1209p'
The upstream condition combines BZ_OK, myfeof(bzf->handle), avail_in == 0
and avail_out > 0, then reports BZ_UNEXPECTED_EOF.  UnZip is already in its
final loop after the compressed ZIP-entry input has been exhausted, replacing
the stdio myfeof condition.  Map the failure to its existing PK_ERR cleanup;
when output is full, continue draining rather than declaring truncation.

References (BZ2_bzRead):
https://sourceware.org/git/?p=bzip2.git;a=blob;f=bzlib.c;hb=bzip2-1.0.6
https://sourceware.org/git/?p=bzip2.git;a=blob;f=bzlib.c;hb=bzip2-1.0.8

--- unzip610c25/extract.c
+++ unzip610c25/extract.c
@@ -6797,6 +6797,12 @@
             DESTROYGLOBALS();
             EXIT(PK_MEM3);
         }
+        /* BZ_OK with spare output space needs more input.  None remains
+         * in this final loop, so report a truncated entry as BZ2_bzRead does.
+         */
+        if (err == BZ_OK && bstrm.avail_in == 0 && bstrm.avail_out > 0) {
+            retval = PK_ERR; goto uzbunzip_cleanup_exit;
+        }
         /* final flush of slide[] */
         if ((retval = FLUSH(wsize - bstrm.avail_out)) != 0)
             goto uzbunzip_cleanup_exit;
